# 9. DELEGATED CHOICE: graphify-out volatile metadata gitignored
Observed after the hook test: every commit triggers the post-commit rebuild, which
rewrites graphify-out/{manifest.json,cache/} with mtime/hash bookkeeping of tracked
files (incl. STATE_PHASE0.md, which changes at every Step boundary) -> committing
those files guarantees an infinite dirty-tree cycle (verified across commits 3359d6d
and 69fb28e). Resolution: semantic outputs (graph.json, GRAPH_REPORT.md, graph.html,
.graphify_labels.json, .graphify_root) remain COMMITTED per roadmap Step 0.1.7;
volatile rebuild metadata (cache/, manifest.json) is gitignored and untracked.
graph.json itself was hash-stable across the no-code-change rebuilds
(cdb07f4f65dee82a...), confirming the ignored files carry no semantic content.
